
Evidence – OWASP ZAP Passive Scan (Observations 6–17)

This folder contains screenshots and supporting evidence collected during the authorized vulnerability assessment of the OWASP Juice Shop local lab.

Tool Used: OWASP ZAP – Passive Scan

Target: http://127.0.0.1:42000/

Observations Covered:

- Observation 6: Content Security Policy (CSP) Header Not Set
- Observation 7: Missing Anti-clickjacking Header
- Observation 8: Session ID in URL Rewrite
- Observation 9: Vulnerable JavaScript Library
- Observation 10: Cross-Domain JavaScript Source File Inclusion
- Observation 11: Private IP Disclosure
- Observation 12: Timestamp Disclosure – Unix
- Observation 13: X-Content-Type-Options Header Missing
- Observation 14: Information Disclosure – Suspicious Comments
- Observation 15: Cross-Domain Misconfiguration (CORS)
- Observation 16: Modern Web Application
- Observation 17: Retrieved from Cache

Purpose:

These screenshots document the alerts identified during passive security testing. Risk levels and confidence values are recorded as reported by OWASP ZAP.

Note: These are scanner observations from a local testing environment. They do not all represent confirmed or exploitable vulnerabilities. Further verification may be required.
